KUBERNETES LEARNING 

Kubernetes is an open source container management platform 

Automates the deployment , management and scaling of container based applications.

Developed at google in 2014 , k8 draws on googles production experience and is now mainatained by the cloud native computing foundation 

it orchestrates containers grouping them into logical units called pods and managing their lifecycle acriss a cluster of machines 

it automatically restarts failed containers , replacrs them when necessary and reschdules workloads onto healthy nodes to maintain the desired state


K8S is like a ship captain for containers , organising placing them on multiple computers like a ship carrying many containers , its introduction will explain key k8s ideas like pods , services and deployments 

Before k8s , docker and docker swarm transformed how developers package applications it  allowed them to bundle an application and its dependencies into a single prtable unit called a container 

this worked fine for small scale deployements but when applications gre to hundered or thousands of containers the following problems appeared 

scalability isssues 
multi cloud deployments 
security and resource management 
rolling updates and zero downtime deployments 

this is the problem k8s was created to solve , it acts as the brain or orchestarator for your containers , handling the complex task of managing them at scale automatically 

