to overcome this , the industry moved toward microservices , where each feature (like payments , serach , or notifications ) is built and deployed independentuly , This made applications more flexible and scalable 

but with microservices came a new challenge instead of running one big app , companies now had to manage hundered or 1000s of small containerized services , containers slved the packaging problem , but without a ways to orchestarte them things got messy , thats where k8s came in acting like a smart manager that automated deployment , scaling coordination of all those microservices 

TERMINOLOGIES IN K8S

POD :

Pod is the smallest unit you can deoloy in K8s , it wraps one or more containers that need to run together , sharing the same network and storage , containers inside a pof can easily communciate and work as a single unit 

NODE :

Node is a machine (physical or virtual) in a k8 cluster that runs your applications , each node containes the tools need to run pods , including the container runtime (like docker ), the kubelet(agent) and the kube proxy (networking)

CLUSTER :

K8s cluster is a grp of comouters (nodes) that work together to run your containerized applicatuons , these nodes can be real machines or virtual one 

2 types of nodes in k0s cluster : 

1. Master node (control plane) : 

think of it as the brain of the cluster 
it makes decisions , like where to run applications , handles scheduling and keeps track of everything

2. Worker nodes : 

these are the machines that actually run your appss inside containers 
each worker node has a kubelet (agent) , a container runtime (like docker or containerd) and tools for networking monitioring 

DEPLOYMET 

Deployment is a k8s object used to manage a set of pods running your containerized applications , it provides declarative updates , meaning you tell k8s what your want , and it figures out how to get there 

REPLICASET 

Replicaset ensures that the right number of identical pods are running 

SERVICES 

A service in k8s is a way to connect applications runnning inside your cluster , it gives your pods a stable way to communicate , even if the pods themselved keep changing 

INGRESS 

Ingress is a way to manage external access to your services in a k8s cluster , it provides http and https routing to your services , acting as a reverse proxy 

CONFIG MAP 

Config map stores configuration settings sepearetly from the application , so changes can be made without modifying actual code 

imagine you have an application that needs some settings like a db password or an api key , instead of hardcoding these settings into your app , you store them in a config map , your application can then read thsese settings from the configmap , your application can then read these settings from the config map at runtime , which makes it easy to update the settings without changing the app code 

SECRET 

A Secret is a way to store sensitive information(like password , api keys or tokens)  securely in a k8s cluster 

PERSISTENT VOLUME (PV)

A PV in k8s is a piece of storage in the cluster that you can use to store data and it doesnt get deleted when pod is removed or restarted 

KUBELET

Kubelet runs on each worked node and ensures pods are running as expected 

KUBE PROXY 

Manages networking inside the cluster , ensuring diff pods can communicate 


KUBERNETES ARCHITECTURE 

K8S follows a client server arch consisting of a control plane (master)  and worker nodes , the control plane includes components such as the api server , schduler , contriller manaegr and etcd for the cluster state storage

worker nodes run application owrkloads and include kubelet for cmmunication with the control plane , kube proxy for networking and a container runtime , such as conatinered docker to manage containers 

CONTROL PLANE COMPONENTS 

It is basically a collection of various compnents that help us in managing the over all health of a cluster , for e.g if you want to set up new pods , destry pods , scale pods etc , bassically 4 services run on the contril plane 

KUBE API SERVER 

The api server is a component of the k8s control plane that exposes the k8s api , it is like an initial gateway tp the cluster that listens to updates or qeries via cli like kubectl 

kubectl communicates with API server to inform what needs to be done like creating pods or deleting pods etc it also works as a gate keeper

it generally validates requests recieved and then forwards them to other processes 

no request can be directly passed to the cluster it has to be passed through the api server 

KUBE SCHEDULER 

Watches for newly created pods that have no assigned node 
selects the best worker node for a pod based on resoruces requirements policy constratints and hardware/software limits

KUBE CONTROLLER MANAGER 

Runs controller processes that maintain the "desired state" of the cluster 
NOde Controller : monitors node health 

Replication controller: ensures the correct number of pod replicac are running 

ETCD

A consistent high availability key value store 
stores all cluster data (the "source of truth") if it isnt in etcd , it doesnt exixt in kubernetes 

WORKER NODE COMPONENTS 

These are the nodes where the actual work happens , each node can have multiple pods and pods have containers running inside them , there are 3 processes in every node that are used to schdule and manage those pods , the following are the some of the components related to node:

1.Container runtime 

the software responsible for actually running the containers 
it pulls images from a registry ans starts/stops the containers 

2.Kubelet

an agent that runs on each node in the cluster 
ensures that containers are running in a pod by following onstructions(podspecs) from the comtrol plane 
reports health and status of the node back to the API server 

3.kube proxy 

a network proxy that maintains network rules on nodes 
allows network communication to your pods frm inside or outside of the cluster
handles service discovery dand load balancing 

