contianers share the same host kernel but are isolated from each other through private namespace and resource contril mechansims at th OS LEVEL , container based virtualisation provides a diff level of abstraction in terms of virtualisation and isolation when compared with hypervisors 

hypervisiors use a lot of hardware which results in overhead in terms of cirtualuzing hardware and virtual device drivers 

a fill OS runs on top of this virtualized hardware in each virtual machine instance 

nut in cintrast containers implement isolation of processed at the OS level , thus avoiding such overhead , these continers run on top of the same shared maOS kernel of the underlying host macine and one or more processes can be run within each container , in containers you dont have to allicate ram it allcates dynamically during creation of containers while in VMS you need to first pre allocate the memory and then created the VM 

